<!-- Added by Plutext Pty Ltd for the docx4j FO renderer (docx4j-fo-renderer), a modified distribution derived
     from Apache FOP 2.12: fox:top-space, hook box-top-space (fop/CR-038). -->
<testcase>
  <info>
    <p>
      fox:top-space on an absolutely positioned block-container names the part of its top that stands for its anchor's
      space-before; where the block opens the column, what the page dropped of that space is given back. top is -15pt
      throughout, 3pt below the paragraph's top less 18pt of space. a: the block opens a page and the space is dropped:
      18pt back. b: the space retained: nothing. c: mid-page: nothing. d: 8pt of 18pt retained: 10pt back. e: the space
      on an enclosing block: 18pt back. f: a second paragraph of a container, opening a page: 18pt back. g: the same on
      the page of the first paragraph: nothing. h: mid-page, the space-after above the larger, so the block records no
      space of its own: nothing, which is why the rule looks only at a block that opens the column.
    </p>
  </info>
  <fo>
